<title>USA: Boeing, McDonnell plan special meetings.</title>
<headline>Boeing, McDonnell plan special meetings.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Co and McDonnell Douglas Corp said they plan special shareholder meetings in July to vote on their planned $14 billion merger.</p>
<p>The companies said they plan to hold the meetings simultaneously at their corporate headquarters in Seattle and St. Louis, but no exact date has been set.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Boeing said the merger was on track to close sometime in midsummer.</p>
<p>A McDonnell Douglas spokesman said the shareholder meetings might be held before the deal gets final regulatory approval. The proposed merger is being reviewed by the U.S. Federal Trade Commission and by the European Commission.</p>
<p>((-- Reuters Seattle bureau 206-386-4848))</p>
